From b6548e21fa59091a41cd96dce74b83ef1f515dea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 09:43:37 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] TFEL: device code support in the mathematical and material
 libraries

- TFEL_DEVICE_CODE macro, defined when device code is compiled, and
  host/device annotations of the mathematical objects, of the fixed size
  algorithms, of the eigen solvers of symmetric tensors (FSES included),
  of the non linear solvers and of the material tools (bounds checks,
  stress criteria, logarithmic strain handler, slip systems, finite
  strain tangent operators).
- tfel::fail and contract violations reported in device code, where
  exceptions are not supported; no recursion in the computation of the
  eigenvectors of symmetric tensors in device code.
- behaviours without virtual functions (MechanicalBehaviourConcept),
  slip systems built at compile time, trivially copyable classes
  (TrivialGenTypeBase, whose values are built in place,
  getConstantObject).
- numerical type of the generic interfaces: IsAssignableTo for narrower
  floating point types, size of the numerical type of a library read by
  ExternalLibraryManager.
- direct conversions of the derivative of the Kirchhoff stress with
  respect to the deformation gradient (DTAU_DF) or to its increment
  (DTAU_DDF) to the derivative of the first Piola-Kirchhoff stress
  (DPK1_DF), computed column by column without intermediate tangent
  operator (explicit code generated by
  scripts/generate-pk1-derivative-conversions.py of MMM-GPU-Proto), and
  their test.
- FiniteStrainBehaviourTangentOperator: assignment of T2toT2 objects
  (DPK1_DF), as for the other types (thelfer/tfel#1489).
- constructor of the fixed size arrays leaving their values uninitialized
  (tfel::math::uninitialized tag); residual and jacobian of the
  Newton-Raphson algorithm left uninitialized (thelfer/tfel#1491).
- products with tpld, tprd, dCdF and dBdF: the terms associated with
  components null by construction are not computed (SparsityPattern,
  SparseProductExpr, thelfer/tfel#1497).
- TinyMatrixSolve: substitutions in place when the rows are not exchanged
  (thelfer/tfel#1500); LUDecomp: columns treated without the permutation
  until the first row exchange (thelfer/tfel#1501).
- conversions of the finite strain tangent operators computed by explicit
  code, column by column, without intermediate tangent operator nor loop
  based push-forward or pull-back: rewritten specialisations and direct
  conversions (FiniteStrainBehaviourTangentOperatorConverters.ixx,
  generated by tools/FiniteStrainBehaviourTangentOperatorConverters,
  whose forms were chosen by measurements on CPU and GPU, in float and in
  double), and their test.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
